# scripts/.docs-skill-refs-baseline — filename-pinned shrink baseline for
# `check-doc-skill-refs.sh --all-docs` (age-gate-the-ungated-egwt.5).
#
# Each line is a LIVE docs/** path that currently carries a dead `/skill`
# reference (a backtick-slash citation or slash-command heading that does not
# resolve to an existing skills/<dir>). The gate treats these as GRANDFATHERED:
# they are allowed to offend, but the list only shrinks.
#
# The ratchet is two-way:
#   - A NON-baselined live doc that acquires a dead skill ref  -> FAIL (fix it).
#   - A baselined file that no longer offends                  -> FAIL (PRUNE it
#     from this list to lock the gain).
#
# To burn one down: repoint the `/skill` at its live successor, mark the line
# retired/folded/legacy/historical, and then delete the file's line here.
#
# dyr0-owned / owner-locked pages (docs/getting-started/**, docs/comparisons/**,
# receipts/proof pages, README/PRODUCT/GOALS) stay baselined if they offend —
# do NOT edit those to burn them down.
#
# Comments (#...) and blank lines are ignored. Keep this list sorted.
